description: Upgrades existing websites and apps to premium quality. Audits current design, identifies generic AI patterns, and applies high-end design standards without breaking functionality. Works with any CSS framework or vanilla CSS.

# Redesign Existing Projects Skill

## Overview
A comprehensive redesign skill that audits existing codebases, identifies generic patterns, and applies targeted premium upgrades without breaking functionality. Works with Tailwind, vanilla CSS, styled-components, or any framework.

## Workflow
1. **Scan** - Read codebase, identify framework and current patterns
2. **Diagnose** - Run design audit across typography, color, layout, interactivity, content
3. **Fix** - Apply targeted upgrades working with the existing stack

## Design Audit Categories

### Typography
- Replace browser default fonts with premium options (Geist, Outfit, Satoshi)
- Increase headline presence with tighter tracking and reduced line-height
- Limit body text width to ~65 characters
- Add Medium (500) and SemiBold (600) weights

### Color & Surfaces
- Replace pure black with off-black/dark charcoal
- Desaturate accent colors (below 80%)
- Pick ONE accent color and stick with it
- Tint shadows to match background hue
- Add subtle noise/grain textures

### Layout
- Break symmetry with offset margins and mixed aspect ratios
- Replace 3-column feature cards with asymmetric grids
- Use min-h-[100dvh] instead of h-screen
- Use CSS Grid instead of complex flexbox math

### Interactivity
- Add hover states, active/pressed feedback
- Smooth transitions (200-300ms)
- Skeleton loaders instead of spinners
- Empty states and error states

## Fix Priority
1. Font swap (biggest instant improvement)
2. Color palette cleanup
3. Hover and active states
4. Layout and spacing
5. Replace generic components
6. Add loading/empty/error states
7. Polish typography scale and spacing

## Rules
- Work with existing tech stack, don't migrate
- Don't break existing functionality
- Check dependency files before importing libraries
- Keep changes reviewable and focused

